.TH NABU 8 "27 August 2026" "nabu-branch-manager 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
nabu \- inspect and switch the Nabu CORE branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nabu branch
.br
.B nabu branch status
.br
.B nabu branch list
.br
.B nabu branch
.RI stable | alpha | unstable
.SH DESCRIPTION
The nabu command selects exactly one CORE branch meta package. Stable uses the
supported 6.17 kernel, alpha uses the isolated 6.17 test kernel and unstable
uses the Rawhide-only 7.2 mainline WIP kernel.
.PP
The canonical subcommand is branch. The common spellings brunch and brucnh
are accepted as compatibility aliases.
.PP
Switching invokes dnf5 through sudo, regenerates the selected UKI and does not
reboot automatically. Existing install-only kernel payloads may remain as
fallback boot entries. The command does not alter sudo policy or grant users
additional privileges.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Non-zero indicates an invalid command, unavailable
branch, failed package transaction, inconsistent branch selection or failed
UKI preparation.
